---1936831473-1406184442-936141385=:72130
Content-Type: TEXT/PLAIN; charset=US-ASCII

I really haven't finished making a good configuration file for tripwire
for my AlphaStations, but I have had quite a few requests for my results.

So I have attached my latest version, which was mostly supplied by Tom
Webster, with ideas from several others.  I still am not handling Netscape
Server logs properly, and have a few other places that change often but
are not security problems.

I did put in a symbol that is left undefined when the /usr/local is on a
shared NFS drive - speeds up the scan considerably.  I want to be able to
use this one file on multiple systems (currently I have 2).

Use at your own risk!

