The consenus of the right way to do this is:

1. Make sure Patch Kit 3 is installed, in partcular the following patch:

Patch 392.02

setld -i |grep 39202
OSFPAT00039202425    installed  Patch: AdvFS Consolidated Patch (Filesystem
Patches)

2. Run in Single user mode, defragment  the domain first

3. Still in single-user mode, fuser -cu /mountpoint to make sure that no
process is accessing data on the domain

4. do the rmvol

Without the patch, rmvol will fail when encountering a "hole" and trying to
move it.

