Dear all,

I've sent an SOS to this list a few days ago because I could not succeed
in installing ImageMagick-4.2.8 on my Alphaserver, and got no answer.

I got the fix from the IM list: it appears that the Makefiles are broken
for the Alpha boxes. This will probably be corrected soon but in the
meantime Bob Friesenham sent me updated makefiles that solve the
problem. His file makes.tar.gz is attached to this message.


1) cd to the parent directory of ImageMagick-4.2.8
2) put the makes.tar.gz there
3) 'gunzip' and 'tar xvf'
   This will replace the broken makefiles
4) cd ImageMagick-4.2.8
5) rm config.cache
6) ./configure
   make
   make install


This will make it.

Cheers,

Jean-Loup


