Morjens,

I had a question about decryption with crypt(3) (see below). The result was to
either search for the corresponding package in the SPD, or use one of the 
freely available crypt replacements like ufc-crypt. Since I could not find the 
package on my lastest SPD we decided to go for ufc-crypt which works just 
fine. Thanks to Spider Boardman, Tom Webster and Alan of DEC.

Original message:

> one of our developers is trying to use crypt(3) functions for decryption. 
> The function always returns ENOSYS which means, according to the man-page 
> crypt(3), that the optional encryption software is not present.
> What am I missing, where do I find the optional encryption software ?


cheers

