From tru64-unix-managers  Wed Aug 18 18:25:02 1999
From: Frank Wortner <frank () bondnet ! com>
Date: Wed, 18 Aug 1999 18:25:02 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: How to Delete Patch Backups?
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079067216046

In an earlier message,  I asked how I could delete the patch backups in
/usr/var/adm/patch/backup in an "approved" manner.  The answer seems to be,
"Make several verified backup copies,  then 'rm
/usr/var/adm/patch/backup/*.'"  Considering that the mailing list archives
at http://www.ornl.gov/its/archives/mailing-lists/ contain several instances
of software installations that backed out patches and refused to install if
this couldn't be done :-(,  keeping a backup around until a full upgrade
might not be a bad idea.

Thanks to Michael Bucholtz [mbucholtz@ceiss.org], Alan Davis
[Davis@Tessco.Com], and Bruce B. Platt [bbp@comport.com] for the advice.

Frank

