Dear Tru64-Admins, 

I had asked for hints when assigning Tru64 versions 4.0D and 
5.0 to a DEC3000_500 and a DEC2100_C500, the one "lagging 
behind" and the other "keeping in front" of the OS versions. 

I received comments from 
      "Dr. Tom Blinn, 603-884-0646" <tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com> 
and   alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com 
(and of course thank them for replying). 

They both agreed in these points: 
- I should not stay with version 4.0B, even though there is no 
  list available _what_ will really fail with years 2000 and higher. 
- It is no sound approach to take binaries from a higher version 
  of Tru64 and expect them to work on a lower one, whether the 
  version difference is in the number or just the letter. 
- Neither of them expected problems with either of these machines 
  and either of the Tru64 versions. 
  However, Dr. Blinn recommended to check support for the graphics 
  adapter with 5.0. Quote: "Most TURBOchannel graphics support 
  has been dropped from V5.0." 
  (This leaves me with the problem to get information on the 
  graphics cards used ...) 

