To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: SUMMARY: Using netgroups with medium sized groups
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079067215985

Dear Tru64 Managers,

Problem: NIS falls over in a heap if records in /etc/netgroup are
bigger than 1024 characters.

Thanks are due to 
	Paul A Sand
	Mike Iglesias
	Toby Bluhm
	Daniel S. Riley
	Barry Branch
	Grant Ward
who all made basically the same suggestion, which is to split big
netgroups into subgroups, e.g.

third-year-ugrads1 (-,adriant,) ....
third-year-ugrads2 (-,draiant,) ....
...
third-year-ugrads third-year-ugrads1 third-year-ugrads2 ...


Since my netgroups file is generated automatically by a script I need
to make this script somewhat cleverer. Mike Iglesias and Paul Sand
helpfully provided some Perl which they use at their site to achieve
this.

My experience with this problem confirms my view that NIS is not the
sweetest-smelling part of the Unix garden!

Regards,
Bob
