From: Jim Belonis <belonis@dirac.phys.washington.edu>

Real NIS and C2 ARE incompatible.  C2 uses a non-NIS back channel to update
the passwd file with the login time.  This requires the network to the master
NIS server to be up and working, so any benefit of having slave servers
is negated, creating a nice bottleneck if you have a large number of users.

And non-DEC NIS servers can not be included in the scheme because of this
special back channel.
And maybe non-DEC clients cause difficulty too.

> HI, Ok, I will not go from nis to c2 , thanks for the warnings of Dr. Tom
> Blinn, Nick Leonard and John Francini.  I must mention that nis and c2 are
> not mutually exclusive as Dr. Tom Blinn said,he and J. Francini also
> adviced to move to min version 4.0D . Nick warned me to take my own peril

