From tru64-unix-managers  Mon Aug 02 13:47:40 1999
From: Henry Joy McCRACKEN <hjmcc () iap ! fr>
Date: Mon, 02 Aug 1999 13:47:40 +0000
To: tru64-unix-managers
Subject: Summary: external drive + second SCSI bus
X-MARC-Message: https://marc.info/?l=tru64-unix-managers&m=96079067215759


Dear Managers, 

Many thanks to the many people who (very quickly!) responded to my
problem --

alan@nabeth.cxo.dec.com
sean@stat.Duke.EDU
tpb@doctor.zk3.dec.com
hall_t@lxe.com
nayle@ncsbah.com
(I think that's everybody)

which was my external drive on a separate SCSI bus was not being
recogized by my xp1000 on booting.

The answer involves doing a kernel config and booting the system with
the new kernel (something I'd done under linux but not had the
opportunity to try with DU):

boot -fl s -fi "genvmunix"
doconfig
(copy vmunix.new to vmunix)
(boot system with new kernel)

I tried this procedure and it worked fine. 

thanks again to everybody that answered, 

henry mccracken
LAS, Marseille

