Hi Managers

I remember a similar posting, but I couldn't find the summary..now I =
have a somewhat similar situation.

in one of our AS4100/4.0D/PK3/firmware 5.4 ,the vdump works fine..when i =
try to vrestore in a blank system ..for e.g say new harddisk.i am =
getting the following errors.

cam_logger: CAM_ERROR packet
            cam_logger: bus 2 target 5 lun 0
            isp_process_response_queue
            Autosence did not occur after check condition
            Active CCB at time of error
            cam_logger: CAM_ERROR packet
            cam_logger: bus 0 target 5 lun 0
            ctape_iodone
            Hard Error Detected
            Seagate AIT 03j0
            Active CCB at time of error
            CCB request completed with error
            error exception or abnormal condition
            ILLEGAL REQUEST-ILLEGAL REQUEST OR CPB PARAMETERS


this happens at the end of vrestore, (The system comes up after this =
restore)..but the error message makes me think that the vrestore may not =
be fully working.

I did like this..

1.take a vdump when a system is alive..
2.remove system disks and install new ones
3.boot from cd-rom=20
4.create device files
5.vrestore from tapes

will summarize. Thanks in Advance



